keep up with changing technologies, enhance collaboration between front-end and back-end developers, and challenge product managers in new ways.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/867b369907ca439b50ed78bc27759146?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-04T15:46:15.814Z"},{"id":"MaDuaB3Xy","title":"Redesigning navigation with a user-centric approach","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/redesigning-navigation-with-a-user-centric-approach-e2e9a4c728ae","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/redesigning-navigation-with-a-user-centric-approach-maduab3xy","summary":"The Product team faced difficulties integrating new features in their B2B product and decided to design a new navigation menu component with a user-centric approach. They used Maze to consult users along the way and validated the architecture through card sorting and tree tests. The main takeaways from the process were the importance of validating the architecture before designing the experience, involving users in the decision-making process, and improving communication with other teams.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a8c1179aa47d0cbcf682105b75e30470?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-27T14:01:43.027Z"},{"id":"EV9IvfwZu","title":"The story behind the creation of our dedicated automation team","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/the-story-behind-the-creation-of-our-dedicated-automation-team-de94e342607a","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-story-behind-the-creation-of-our-dedicated-automation-team-ev9ivfwzu","summary":"The creation of a dedicated automation team at WTTJ improved efficiency, saved time, and eliminated manual tasks for various internal teams. Challenges faced by the customer onboarding team in 2023 led to the formation of the automation team. The team implemented processes, selected technology stack, and focused on bug fixing and scaling. The team aims to provide coaching, training, and expand their expertise to other teams in the future.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b4a6823e3fc2cede9c7979353f0e6a72?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-22T15:38:02.217Z"},{"id":"wctf4TtnG","title":"Why taking notes can be beneficial for you and others","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/why-taking-notes-can-be-beneficial-for-you-and-others-9337235ebf62?source=rss----ffa998e8faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-taking-notes-can-be-beneficial-for-you-and-others-wctf4ttng","summary":"Taking notes can be beneficial for personal growth as it helps minimize errors, improves understanding, allows for delving deeper into topics, and helps avoid impostor syndrome.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eeaa8e1f66dbd187b6344599a0dda890?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-05T12:18:32.734Z"},{"id":"dwEldAU0v","title":"Debug my job #1 \u2014 Am\u00e9lie, Product writer and Localization specialist","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/debug-my-job-1-am%C3%A9lie-product-writer-and-localization-specialist-1dd6935cd05d?source=rss----ffa998e8faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/debug-my-job-1-am-lie-product-writer-and-localization-specialist-dweldau0v","summary":"Learn about the role of a UX writer and the importance of hiring one for tech companies. Discover the skills necessary for a product writer and the challenges they face in their job.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/544201ef57e0217a54f9d5f6b4e88cec?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-07T12:16:56.332Z"},{"id":"LQLkIG4A6","title":"Choosing the right analytics tool: Insights from our Contentsquare journey","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/choosing-the-right-analytics-tool-insights-from-our-contentsquare-journey-e814f7cbfe5b?source=rss----ffa998e8faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/choosing-the-right-analytics-tool-insights-from-our-contentsquare-journey-lqlkig4a6","summary":"This article discusses the journey of Welcome to the Jungle (WTTJ) in selecting and implementing Contentsquare as their analytics tool. The article highlights the limitations of their previous tool, Snowplow, and explains the process they went through to choose Contentsquare. It also mentions key functionalities of Contentsquare that meet their needs, such as optimized data implementation, user-friendly interface, zoning feature, and advanced segmentation. The article concludes by discussing the challenges and benefits of using Contentsquare and the company's commitment to data-driven decision-making.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/16aa9f5ae6feb1022763d84d9121be9f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-19T07:45:28.112Z"},{"id":"FxbVv5BC2","title":"Exploring various approaches for testing external calls in Elixir","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/exploring-various-approaches-for-testing-external-calls-in-elixir-4f22e8c8fdae?source=rss----ffa998e8faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/exploring-various-approaches-for-testing-external-calls-in-elixir-fxbvv5bc2","summary":"This article explores various approaches for testing external calls in Elixir, including monkey patching, using a fake HTTP server, employing mocks with behavior, and utilizing Mox. It discusses the strengths and limitations of each method and emphasizes the importance of testing business logic.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/752aa93697de8b0210048416331f3389?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-02T07:53:50.056Z"},{"id":"p1xwNG2sr","title":"Observability: Reducing noise in Elixir applications","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/observability-reducing-noise-in-elixir-applications-5bd39d494101?source=rss----ffa998e8faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/observability-reducing-noise-in-elixir-applications-p1xwng2sr","summary":"Observability refers to the ability to monitor and analyze the health of an application\u2019s system. Three types of data are aggregated to achieve observability: logs, metrics, and traces. This article is aimed at experienced Elixir developers looking to improve their observability practices.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b932cbc161ae4fc994f4bd9fbcd06b64?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-18T07:27:03.416Z"},{"id":"wlX9csuXh","title":"The benefits of using Elixir for backend development: Our perspective","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/the-benefits-of-using-elixir-for-backend-development-our-perspective-9d421fde426a?source=rss----ffa998e8faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-benefits-of-using-elixir-for-backend-development-our-perspective-wlx9csuxh","summary":"This post discusses the benefits of using Elixir for backend development, including its resilience, functional nature, and similarities to Ruby on Rails. It also highlights the challenges and limitations of using Elixir, such as recruitment difficulties and a smaller community.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3dd83e2530c3d3cbec54bd3e37c131fd?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-06T10:16:17.923Z"},{"id":"RN9mwrEfM","title":"The 3 features that will make you fall for Elixir","url":"https://medium.com/wttj-tech/the-3-features-that-will-make-you-fall-for-elixir-598c9a31172d?source=rss----ffa998e8faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-3-features-that-will-make-you-fall-for-elixir-rn9mwrefm","summary":"Discover the features of Elixir that make it elegant and efficient! Explore pattern matching, unit testing, and concurrency in this beginner-friendly guide.",